WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.835 --> 00:00:09.159
Tom Lindqvist: Morning, both. How's Denver treating you this week?

2
00:00:09.951 --> 00:00:15.765
Brandon Hughes: Pretty good. Busy. We're heading into the fall promo push so it's all hands.

3
00:00:16.965 --> 00:00:25.310
Michelle Tran: Same here. I've got two new folks starting on the Genesys side next Monday, so I'm mostly doing training prep right now.

4
00:00:25.542 --> 00:00:29.365
Tom Lindqvist: Nice. Are they going straight onto the sales queues?

5
00:00:30.696 --> 00:00:36.888
Michelle Tran: One of them, yeah. The other is going to the billing side first, then we'll see.

6
00:00:37.291 --> 00:00:47.894
Tom Lindqvist: Got it. Before we get into anything else, how are the call volumes looking? Last time we talked you were around the mid-forty-thousands a month.

7
00:00:48.714 --> 00:00:54.927
Brandon Hughes: We're a bit above that now. August came in around fifty-one thousand, and September is tracking similar.

8
00:00:55.948 --> 00:00:57.708
Tom Lindqvist: That's a decent jump.

9
00:00:58.665 --> 00:01:06.667
Brandon Hughes: Yeah, the fiber bundle campaign is doing well. Google Ads is spending more, so more calls are coming in.

10
00:01:07.347 --> 00:01:11.387
Tom Lindqvist: And the offline conversions are still landing in Google Ads okay?

11
00:01:11.954 --> 00:01:16.050
Brandon Hughes: Far as I know, yeah. Nothing's come up on that.

12
00:01:16.728 --> 00:01:25.053
Tom Lindqvist: Good. Michelle, I wanted to check in on the PreSense side. You flagged something a couple weeks back about screen pops.

13
00:01:25.561 --> 00:01:37.723
Michelle Tran: I did, and it's still happening. Here's the thing. When Genesys transfers a call from one queue to another, or from one agent to another, the receiving agent gets a blank screen pop.

14
00:01:37.723 --> 00:01:38.828
Michelle Tran: Nothing in it.

15
00:01:39.317 --> 00:01:42.925
Tom Lindqvist: So the pop fires, it just has no data in it.

16
00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:57.947
Michelle Tran: Right. The agent sees the PreSense window come up but there's no journey, no pages, no ad. So they end up asking the caller what they were looking at, which is exactly what we bought this to avoid.

17
00:01:58.501 --> 00:02:00.193
Tom Lindqvist: How often is it happening?

18
00:02:00.889 --> 00:02:11.863
Michelle Tran: It's not every transfer, but it's often enough that my supervisors are noticing. Probably a handful a day per queue, more on the busier ones.

19
00:02:12.631 --> 00:02:19.494
Brandon Hughes: It's coming up in our sales huddles too. The agents on the receiving end are the ones complaining.

20
00:02:19.878 --> 00:02:23.852
Tom Lindqvist: Okay. Is it specific to certain queues, or is it any transfer?

21
00:02:24.999 --> 00:02:32.495
Michelle Tran: Any transfer as far as I can tell. We tried it on the wireless queue and the fiber queue, same result.

22
00:02:33.474 --> 00:02:38.046
Tom Lindqvist: And is this happening on warm transfers, cold transfers, or both?

23
00:02:39.141 --> 00:02:42.656
Michelle Tran: Both. We tested it with a couple of supervisors watching.

24
00:02:44.038 --> 00:02:56.742
Tom Lindqvist: Got it. I want to get this in front of the right folks with the details you just gave me. Can you send me a couple of call IDs where it happened?

25
00:02:56.742 --> 00:02:58.727
Tom Lindqvist: That'll help them trace it.

26
00:03:00.144 --> 00:03:02.606
Michelle Tran: Yeah, I can pull those this afternoon.

27
00:03:02.908 --> 00:03:13.218
Tom Lindqvist: Perfect. I'll take it back to the team and see what we can find out. I won't promise anything on timing yet, but I'll keep you posted.

28
00:03:14.037 --> 00:03:15.519
Michelle Tran: That works. Thanks, Tom.

29
00:03:15.937 --> 00:03:17.940
Tom Lindqvist: Anything else on the list today?

30
00:03:18.995 --> 00:03:27.563
Brandon Hughes: I think we're good. Oh, one thing. Can we move our next check-in to the Tuesday instead of Wednesday? I've got a conflict that week.

31
00:03:28.985 --> 00:03:35.236
Tom Lindqvist: Sure, I'll send a new invite. Anything else, or should I let you both get back to it?

32
00:03:36.571 --> 00:03:38.930
Michelle Tran: That's it from me. Talk soon.

33
00:03:39.395 --> 00:03:41.439
Tom Lindqvist: Sounds good. Thanks, both. Talk soon.
